    "line": 16,
    "severity": "low",
    "summary": "API fixture leaves titles random (setup_bookmark default), so title order is not controlled and a wrong sort mapping could pass by chance",
    "failure_scenario": "Suppose an implementation wrongly maps modified_asc to order_by('title'). The three titles come from get_random_string, so 1 run in 6 sorts them as b, c, a. When that happens, test_list_bookmarks_sort_modified_asc passes even though the code is broken. Giving the bookmarks fixed titles whose order differs from every expected order (as the e2e fixture does with Alpha/Bravo/Charlie) removes the chance."
   },
   {
    "file": "bookmarks/tests/test_sort_by_modified_api.py",
    "line": 77,
    "severity": "low",
    "summary": "The unknown-sort fallback test also passes on the code before the change, which the strategy says every test must not do",
    "failure_scenario": "On base 0837b51, ?sort=bogus already falls back to -date_added, so this test is green both before and after the change. That is expected for a 'still falls back' regression criterion, but it should be labelled as a regression guard and not counted as evidence that the feature works. Its fixture does separate the default order from added_asc and both modified orders, so a fallback that silently switched to one of those would be caught."
   }
